runtime-3: bound the tail of forced tool calls (whitespace runaway to max_tokens).

Research experiment for docs/research/deepinfer/runtime.md runtime-3. NOT in patches/series.
Off unless VLLM_TOOL_CALL_BOUND=1; with it unset (or anything but 1) get_model_structural_tag
builds exactly the structural tag it builds today.

The fault (docs/vllm-0.31.md, "What is still unproven"): a forced get_time call decodes
whitespace after <function=get_time> until max_tokens, 1-2 of 20 seeds on 0.31.0. In the image
the qwen_3_coder builtin tag is compiled with max_whitespace_cnt=None, so the argument grammar
of a tool with no parameters is root ::= [ \n\r\t]* and xgrammar accepts the call with 2,000
newlines inside it; with tool_choice=required (TriggeredTagsFormat, at_least_one, parallel
calls) any text may also follow </tool_call> until EOS. xgrammar's disable_any_whitespace is
JSON-only and does not reach either.

With VLLM_TOOL_CALL_BOUND=1, for tool_choice required or named (never auto), xgrammar builtin
models only:
  - max_whitespace_cnt=VLLM_TOOL_CALL_MAX_WS (default 16) caps every whitespace run in the
    argument grammar; qwen_xml string values (TagDispatch) are not affected, so code with deep
    indentation inside a <parameter> still matches;
  - required's TriggeredTagsFormat becomes TagsWithSeparatorFormat(separator="\n") followed by
    at most VLLM_TOOL_CALL_MAX_WS whitespace characters, after which only EOS is legal. This is
    the grammar-level form of DeepInfer's bound (structure_output/matcher.py): the output ends at
    </tool_call> instead of admitting a free tail.
Behaviour change when on: text after a required call is no longer allowed (it was returned as
content); a pretty-printed JSON argument deeper than 16 whitespace characters is forced compact.

Kind: experiment
Cut-against: ghcr.io/syv-ai/hyperqwen:latest site-packages/vllm (0.31.0 + patches/series)
Apply: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz 0 -d <site-packages/vllm> -i runtime3-tool-call-bound.patch

